short_label: VII.13
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If four numbers are proportional, then they are also proportional alternately.
----
proof:

Let the four numbers *A, B, C,* and *D* be proportional, so that *A* is to *B* as *C* is to *D.*

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="150" height="230" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VII.13 diagram" src="propVII13.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "VII.13",
        elements: [
            "A0;point;free;30,-1000;0;0",
            "A3;point;free;30,1000;0;0",
            "A1;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,30,30;0",
            "B0;point;free;60,-1000;0;0",
            "B3;point;free;60,1000;0;0",
            "B1;point;lineSlider;B0,B3,60,30;0",
            "C0;point;free;90,-1000;0;0",
            "C3;point;free;90,1000;0;0",
            "C1;point;lineSlider;C0,C3,90,30;0",
            "D0;point;free;120,-1000;0;0",
            "D3;point;free;120,1000;0;0",
            "D1;point;lineSlider;D0,D3,120,30;0",
            "A2;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,30,200;0",
            "A;line;connect;A1,A2;black",
            "B2;point;lineSlider;B0,B3,60,120;0",
            "B;line;connect;B1,B2;black",
            "C2;point;lineSlider;C0,C3,90,175;0",
            "C;line;connect;C1,C2;black",
            "D2;point;proportion;A1,A2,B1,B2,C1,C2,D1,D3;0",
            "D;line;connect;D1,D2;black"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

I say that they are also proportional alternately, so that *A* is to *C* as *B* is to *D.*

Since *A* is to *B* as *C* is to *D,* therefore, *A* is the same part or parts of *B* as *C* is of *D.* [!just VII.Def.20]

Therefore, alternately, *A* is the same part or parts of *C* as *B* is of *D.* [!just VII.10]

Therefore *A* is to *C* as *B* is to *D.* [!just VII.Def.20]

Therefore, *if four numbers are proportional, then they are also proportional alternately.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
<br clear="all">
----
guide:

This is the numerical analogue of proposition @V.16 for magnitudes. It says that

<center>if <i>a</i> : <i>b</i> = <i>c</i> : <i>d,</i> then <i>a</i> : <i>c</i> = <i>b</i> : <i>d.</i></center>

This proposition is used frequently in Books VII through IX starting with the next proposition.
